  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the single-page modern portfolio website for your profile as an Associate Software Engineer & ECM Technical Consultant. \n\nThe core requirements have been fully addressed:\n- **Tech Stack Setup**: The workspace was automatically bootstrapped with Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS v4, and `lucide-react`. I\'ve additionally installed `next-themes` and `motion/react` to support your requirements.\n- **Project Structure**: Created a scalable, modular architecture with dedicated components for navigation, layouts, and discrete page sections.\n- **Dark/Light Mode**: Implemented a responsive navigation bar with a seamless `next-themes` driven dark/light mode toggle.\n- **Section Implementations**:\n  - **Hero**: An attention-grabbing introduction utilizing Framer Motion entrance animations.\n  - **About & Skills**: A structured grid layout highlighting your education, certifications, and skills matrix.\n  - **Experience**: An anonymized, timeline-style breakdown of your ECM and backend consulting roles.\n  - **Projects**: A clean grid highlighting your independent backend, utility, and full-stack projects.\n  - **Blog**: A mock technical blog section ready for CMS or markdown integration.\n  - **Contact**: A fully integrated Formspree contact form with submission state handling.\n\n### **Folder Structure**\n```text\n/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 globals.css          # Tailwind imports and base styles\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout.tsx           # Root layout with ThemeProvider injection\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 page.tsx             # Main page aggregating all modular sections\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 header.tsx           # Sticky navigation with mobile menu and theme toggle\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 footer.tsx           # Footer with social links\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme-provider.tsx   # next-themes wrapper\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme-toggle.tsx     # Light/Dark mode switcher\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 sections/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hero.tsx         # Hero introduction\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 about.tsx        # Education and Skills Matrix\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 experience.tsx   # Professional Experience timeline\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 projects.tsx     # Independent Projects grid\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 blog.tsx         # Technical Blog preview\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 contact.tsx      # Formspree Contact form\n```\n\nThe application is now live in your preview window. You can freely toggle between themes and view the layout on both desktop and mobile resolutions to see the responsive design in action."
    modified_response: "I have completed the single-page modern portfolio website for your profile as an Associate Software Engineer & ECM Technical Consultant. \n\nThe core requirements have been fully addressed:\n- **Tech Stack Setup**: The workspace was automatically bootstrapped with Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS v4, and `lucide-react`. I\'ve additionally installed `next-themes` and `motion/react` to support your requirements.\n- **Project Structure**: Created a scalable, modular architecture with dedicated components for navigation, layouts, and discrete page sections.\n- **Dark/Light Mode**: Implemented a responsive navigation bar with a seamless `next-themes` driven dark/light mode toggle.\n- **Section Implementations**:\n  - **Hero**: An attention-grabbing introduction utilizing Framer Motion entrance animations.\n  - **About & Skills**: A structured grid layout highlighting your education, certifications, and skills matrix.\n  - **Experience**: An anonymized, timeline-style breakdown of your ECM and backend consulting roles.\n  - **Projects**: A clean grid highlighting your independent backend, utility, and full-stack projects.\n  - **Blog**: A mock technical blog section ready for CMS or markdown integration.\n  - **Contact**: A fully integrated Formspree contact form with submission state handling.\n\n### **Folder Structure**\n```text\n/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 globals.css          # Tailwind imports and base styles\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout.tsx           # Root layout with ThemeProvider injection\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 page.tsx             # Main page aggregating all modular sections\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 header.tsx           # Sticky navigation with mobile menu and theme toggle\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 footer.tsx           # Footer with social links\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme-provider.tsx   # next-themes wrapper\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme-toggle.tsx     # Light/Dark mode switcher\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 sections/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hero.tsx         # Hero introduction\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 about.tsx        # Education and Skills Matrix\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 experience.tsx   # Professional Experience timeline\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 projects.tsx     # Independent Projects grid\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 blog.tsx         # Technical Blog preview\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 contact.tsx      # Formspree Contact form\n```\n\nThe application is now live in your preview window. You can freely toggle between themes and view the layout on both desktop and mobile resolutions to see the responsive design in action."
