  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Redesign Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the project\'s parameters. The core objective is a comprehensive redesign and content realignment of my portfolio. I\'ve already identified the \"Datacap Barcode Injector\" project as something to remove from the content list, which will help streamline the portfolio.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Content & Design**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus to emphasizing ECM expertise, de-emphasizing MERN projects. I\'m moving forward with a dark, minimalist theme with Amber accents. I\'m focusing on UI/UX with framer motion, now looking at how to implement staggerChildren for grids and hover states. I\'m also ensuring that Tailwind is configured correctly in v4.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Style**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dark theme as the default. I\'ve updated `next-themes` to default to dark mode in `app/layout.tsx`. I\'m starting on the sections, like the hero component, where I plan to emphasize ECM, update colors, and add sequence animations. Then I\'ll focus on experience, about, and projects, ensuring stagger animations, hover effects, and updated colors are applied. In the projects section, I will remove \"Datacap Barcode Injector\" and emphasize other enterprise-level projects.\n\n\n**Implementing Color Palette & Stagger**\n\nI\'m making progress on the color updates for the header, footer, blog, and contact sections, removing the blue and focusing on amber. I\'m also planning to incorporate stagger animations into the blog and contact sections for a more dynamic feel. I am setting the default theme to dark.\n\n\n**Enhancing Component Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed updates for the experience and projects sections, emphasizing specific aspects of my ECM expertise and removing outdated projects. I\'m incorporating the staggerChildren animation and hover effects to boost the visual appeal, and I\'m updating the accent colors to amber across these sections. I\'m also planning to revamp the remaining components (header, footer, about, blog, and contact) to streamline the look and feel.\n\n\n**Updating Color & Animation**\n\nI\'m currently replacing all blue-themed Tailwind classes with their amber counterparts across the project. I\'m also preparing to add stagger and hover animations. I\'ve now drafted the `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` for the hero section, emphasizing Java, Datacap, CMOD, and FileNet in the summary. I\'m also planning to rewrite the projects array, prioritizing key ECM projects like the Java Ingestion Service, the Enterprise SOAP Integration, and the CMOD Archival Utility.\n\n\n**Revising Project Content**\n\nI\'m now revising the project descriptions and content, emphasizing my IBM CMOD and Datacap experience. I\'m focusing on the Java and SOAP Integration to improve the project array. I\'m also preparing to refactor the color classes by finding and replacing blue with amber. The hero section needs a complete rewrite.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing color changes and animations across several components. Specifically, I\'m updating the color scheme and adding stagger effects to the about, header, blog, and contact sections. Also, I\'ve updated the theme provider in `app/layout.tsx` to ensure the default theme is dark, improving the overall look and feel. The hero section is where I\'m working with motion and stagger. I\'m also planning to incorporate similar enhancements into the blog and contact sections for a consistent and dynamic experience.\n\n\n\n**Crafting Hero Section Motion**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the motion design of the hero section. I\'m building out the `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` for a smooth animation effect. I\'m working with the motion library to ensure an engaging introduction. I\'m aiming for a visually appealing and dynamic effect.\n\n\n**Defining Hero Component Content**\n\nI\'m now drafting the content for my portfolio\'s hero section, focusing on clear articulation of my ECM expertise. I\'ll highlight my skills, like architecting scalable microservices, Datacap application development, and CMOD infrastructure administration, to engage the user. I plan to use these phrases to convey my strengths.\n\n\n**Refining Contact Section**\n\nI\'m now refining the Contact Me button, applying the same motion effects I\'ve defined elsewhere. I\'m focusing on consistency in animations, which will enhance the overall user experience. I\'m incorporating the motion library to ensure an engaging transition when the user interacts with the button. I\'m also planning a similar motion treatment for the button in the projects section.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Project Highlighting**\n\nI\'m now integrating the updated project array into the projects section. I\'m focusing on showcasing the Java Ingestion Service, CRM & FileTrail SOAP Integration, and IBM CMOD Bulk Archival Utility, highlighting their respective strengths. I\'m ensuring their descriptions align with my overall ECM expertise.\n\n\n**Evaluating Project Showcase**\n\nI\'m now determining which projects should be front and center in my portfolio. I\'m prioritizing the \"IBM Datacap Processing Suite\" to showcase my document automation skills, and I\'ll include the \"JAX-RS Mock Banking API\" for backend development. I plan to refine the descriptions and technologies to resonate with my expertise.\n\n\n**Enhancing Project Presentation**\n\nI\'m now implementing `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` within the projects section to improve the user experience. I\'m leveraging `motion.div` and `motion.ul` to apply stagger animations on each of the projects. I\'m focusing on ensuring these projects and their descriptions are highly visible and impactful, with new emphasis on ECM expertise, just as I plan to do on other sections.\n\n\n**Refining Motion Effects**\n\nI\'m now integrating motion effects into the projects section. I\'ve applied `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` using `motion.div` and `motion.ul` to enable stagger animations, highlighting each project. I\'m prioritizing ECM expertise for each project to streamline the content. My aim is a visually dynamic and engaging showcase.\n\n\n**Optimizing Project Descriptions**\n\nI\'m now revising the project descriptions to showcase expertise and align the project array. I\'m focusing on highlighting the key aspects, the technologies I used, and the impact of each project, for a more appealing and effective showcase of my expertise. I\'m ensuring everything is easy to understand.\n\n\n**Implementing Project Section Refinement**\n\nI\'m now implementing the additional projects in a new section with stagger animations, similar to the main projects. I\'m leveraging `motion.div` and `motion.ul` with `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` for visual consistency. I am ensuring that the project descriptions are also being refined for clarity and alignment with my expertise.\n\n\n**Assessing Experience Showcase**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the best way to showcase my experience section. I am building the structure with visual effects. I\'m focusing on a layout that effectively highlights my professional journey. I plan to use the `motion` library for an enhanced visual flow and dynamic display. The goal is to provide a concise and engaging presentation of my skills and experience.\n\n\n\n**Showcasing Experience Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the experience showcase. I\'m focusing on the `motion` library for an improved layout. I plan to ensure the display is dynamic and engaging with relevant details. I\'m preparing to highlight the consulting role and describe my contributions to digital archiving solutions, with details about FileNet, Datacap, CMOD, and FileTrail integrations. I will also make sure to highlight the Java ingestion service and the end-to-end implementation details.\n\n\n**Refining Experience Presentation**\n\nI\'m now building the experience section. I\'m focusing on dynamic and engaging content with `motion` library, showcasing key details and roles. I\'m organizing the content to highlight contributions to archival and integration solutions, and I\'ll describe FileNet, Datacap, CMOD, and FileTrail implementations. I am working on the visual presentation.\n\n\n**Structuring Experience Details**\n\nI\'m now structuring the work experience section with a heading and a container for individual experience entries. I\'m leveraging the `motion.div` component for stagger effects. The container uses `containerVariants` and `itemVariants`, for animation upon view. The experience details are laid out for optimal readability.\n\n\n\n**Defining Experience Design**\n\nI\'m now building the layout for the work experience entries, leveraging motion for dynamic presentation. The container will utilize `containerVariants` and `itemVariants` to enhance visual flow. I\'m focusing on crafting a responsive and engaging design that\'s easy to read. I\'ll need to define the content, then implement the animations.\n\n\n**Implementing Experience Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dark theme and amber selection colors to experience entries using the motion library for the dark theme. I\'ve updated the colors in `app/layout.tsx`. I will make sure the experience entries are formatted, too. Then, I plan to update the other components.\n\n\n"
