  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully redesigned the portfolio to align strictly with your identity as an ECM Technical Consultant and refined the UI/UX according to your specifications:\n\n- **Enterprise Content Realignment**:\n  - The \"Datacap Barcode Injector\" project has been completely removed.\n  - The Hero section has been rewritten to boldly highlight your ECM expertise, mentioning your work with IBM Datacap, CMOD, FileNet, and SOAP integrations.\n  - The Projects section is now split into two grids: **Enterprise Engineering Work** (front and center, featuring your Java Ingestion Services, CMOD utilities, and CRM integrations) and **Additional Projects** (where the MERN/React apps have been appropriately deprioritized).\n  - The Experience section timelines were adjusted for strong enterprise narrative flow.\n\n- **Sophisticated Dark Theme**:\n  - All traces of the generic blue palette have been stripped out.\n  - The site now defaults to a sleek, monochromatic dark mode (`neutral-950` backgrounds, charcoal cards) with high-contrast, premium **amber** accents (`amber-500` / `amber-600`) reserved exclusively for buttons, active states, and hover effects.\n  - Background blurs were replaced with extremely subtle, minimalist gradient washes that don\'t distract from the content.\n\n- **Framer Motion Interactivity**:\n  - **Sequential Loading**: The Hero text now cascades in elegantly on load.\n  - **Staggered Grids**: The Experience, Enterprise Projects, and Additional Projects grids all utilize `staggerChildren` so the cards gracefully flow into place as you scroll down the page.\n  - **Hover States**: The main enterprise project cards and experience items now feature smooth `<motion.div>` scaling (`scale: 1.02`), subtle upward translations (`y: -5`), and a soft amber ambient shadow glow on hover to make the interface feel tactile and responsive. \n\nThe application is compiled and the preview is live with the new dark aesthetic."
    modified_response: "I have successfully redesigned the portfolio to align strictly with your identity as an ECM Technical Consultant and refined the UI/UX according to your specifications:\n\n- **Enterprise Content Realignment**:\n  - The \"Datacap Barcode Injector\" project has been completely removed.\n  - The Hero section has been rewritten to boldly highlight your ECM expertise, mentioning your work with IBM Datacap, CMOD, FileNet, and SOAP integrations.\n  - The Projects section is now split into two grids: **Enterprise Engineering Work** (front and center, featuring your Java Ingestion Services, CMOD utilities, and CRM integrations) and **Additional Projects** (where the MERN/React apps have been appropriately deprioritized).\n  - The Experience section timelines were adjusted for strong enterprise narrative flow.\n\n- **Sophisticated Dark Theme**:\n  - All traces of the generic blue palette have been stripped out.\n  - The site now defaults to a sleek, monochromatic dark mode (`neutral-950` backgrounds, charcoal cards) with high-contrast, premium **amber** accents (`amber-500` / `amber-600`) reserved exclusively for buttons, active states, and hover effects.\n  - Background blurs were replaced with extremely subtle, minimalist gradient washes that don\'t distract from the content.\n\n- **Framer Motion Interactivity**:\n  - **Sequential Loading**: The Hero text now cascades in elegantly on load.\n  - **Staggered Grids**: The Experience, Enterprise Projects, and Additional Projects grids all utilize `staggerChildren` so the cards gracefully flow into place as you scroll down the page.\n  - **Hover States**: The main enterprise project cards and experience items now feature smooth `<motion.div>` scaling (`scale: 1.02`), subtle upward translations (`y: -5`), and a soft amber ambient shadow glow on hover to make the interface feel tactile and responsive. \n\nThe application is compiled and the preview is live with the new dark aesthetic."
