  user_input {
    user_response: "**CRITICAL UI OVERHAUL: Fix Theme, Colors, and Implement Advanced Mouse Tracking**\n\n**1. Fix Dark/Light Mode & Colors**\n\n* **The Toggle is Broken:** Fix the light/dark mode state management immediately. Implement `next-themes` using a `<ThemeProvider>` wrapper in the root layout to ensure Tailwind\'s `dark:` variants apply correctly to the DOM.\n* **Color Overhaul:** The current palette is unacceptable. Implement a strict, high-contrast minimalist palette:\n* **Dark Mode:** `bg-neutral-950` with `text-neutral-300` for primary text and `text-neutral-500` for secondary text.\n* **Light Mode:** `bg-[#fafafa]` with `text-neutral-900`.\n* **Borders/Accents:** Use 1px solid borders (`border-neutral-800` in dark mode, `border-neutral-200` in light mode). No vibrant blues or tertiary colors anywhere.\n\n\n\n**2. Header Preservation**\n\n* Keep the exact \"Aly.\" text logo in the top left corner. Do not alter its positioning or typography.\n\n**3. Interactive Binary Spotlight Background (Mouse Tracking)**\n\n* Implement a full-screen, fixed background component behind the main content that tracks the cursor.\n* **Binary Grid:** Render a subtle, low-opacity monospaced grid of 0s and 1s across the entire viewport.\n* **Motion Tracking:** Use Framer Motion (`useMotionValue` and `useSpring`) tied to a `mousemove` event listener to track `clientX` and `clientY`.\n* **Flashlight Effect:** Use a dynamic CSS `mask-image: radial-gradient(...)` centered exactly on the cursor\'s coordinates. As the mouse moves, this gradient must act like a flashlight, illuminating the binary code directly beneath the cursor while keeping the rest of the screen entirely minimal and blank. Ensure `pointer-events-none` is applied to this layer so it doesn\'t block UI interactions.\n\n**4. General Polish**\n\n* Ensure the ECM and enterprise architecture projects remain the absolute center of the layout as previously instructed. Do not revert the content."
    items {
      text: "**CRITICAL UI OVERHAUL: Fix Theme, Colors, and Implement Advanced Mouse Tracking**\n\n**1. Fix Dark/Light Mode & Colors**\n\n* **The Toggle is Broken:** Fix the light/dark mode state management immediately. Implement `next-themes` using a `<ThemeProvider>` wrapper in the root layout to ensure Tailwind\'s `dark:` variants apply correctly to the DOM.\n* **Color Overhaul:** The current palette is unacceptable. Implement a strict, high-contrast minimalist palette:\n* **Dark Mode:** `bg-neutral-950` with `text-neutral-300` for primary text and `text-neutral-500` for secondary text.\n* **Light Mode:** `bg-[#fafafa]` with `text-neutral-900`.\n* **Borders/Accents:** Use 1px solid borders (`border-neutral-800` in dark mode, `border-neutral-200` in light mode). No vibrant blues or tertiary colors anywhere.\n\n\n\n**2. Header Preservation**\n\n* Keep the exact \"Aly.\" text logo in the top left corner. Do not alter its positioning or typography.\n\n**3. Interactive Binary Spotlight Background (Mouse Tracking)**\n\n* Implement a full-screen, fixed background component behind the main content that tracks the cursor.\n* **Binary Grid:** Render a subtle, low-opacity monospaced grid of 0s and 1s across the entire viewport.\n* **Motion Tracking:** Use Framer Motion (`useMotionValue` and `useSpring`) tied to a `mousemove` event listener to track `clientX` and `clientY`.\n* **Flashlight Effect:** Use a dynamic CSS `mask-image: radial-gradient(...)` centered exactly on the cursor\'s coordinates. As the mouse moves, this gradient must act like a flashlight, illuminating the binary code directly beneath the cursor while keeping the rest of the screen entirely minimal and blank. Ensure `pointer-events-none` is applied to this layer so it doesn\'t block UI interactions.\n\n**4. General Polish**\n\n* Ensure the ECM and enterprise architecture projects remain the absolute center of the layout as previously instructed. Do not revert the content."
    }
  }
