  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Dark Mode Implementation**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the dark/light mode issue. The user is right, something\'s broken. I\'ve already set up `next-themes` and the provider, but I\'m suspecting the toggle icon might not be updating, or there\'s a hydration glitch. Time to dig deeper and pinpoint the problem.\n\n\n**Analyzing Theme Toggle**\n\nI\'ve examined the code, focusing on `app/layout.tsx`, `components/theme-provider.tsx`, and `components/theme-toggle.tsx`. I\'ve also decided to follow a strict minimalist palette of colors: dark with `bg-neutral-950`, `text-neutral-300`, and `text-neutral-500` (secondary). Light will be  `bg-[#fafafa]`, `text-neutral-900`. I will use 1px solid borders (`border-neutral-800` for dark, `border-neutral-200` for light). I will also remove any amber accents. Lastly, I will preserve the user\'s changes to the ECM projects section.\n\n**Implementing Interactive Background**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive binary spotlight background. I\'m building a full-screen, fixed background with a binary grid, tracking the mouse using Framer Motion (`useMotionValue`, `useSpring`). I\'m creating a flashlight effect with CSS `mask-image: radial-gradient(...)` centered on the cursor, and using `pointer-events-none`.\n\n\n\n**Refining Dark Mode Logic**\n\nI\'ve discovered I hardcoded dark mode in the `html` tag, breaking the theme toggle. I need to remove `\"dark\"` from the `html` tag to fix this. I\'ll need to update `theme-toggle.tsx` to manage hydration issues with `useTheme` and confirm neutral colors are applied. I also have to remove amber accents and start overhauling color palette in the layout to ensure neutrals are followed.\n\n\n**Neutralizing Color Accents**\n\nI\'m removing the amber accent from the \"Aly.\" logo, making it neutral to align with the minimalist theme. I am now working through all sections to replace any amber with neutral colors (including background, borders, and text). I\'m also creating the interactive binary spotlight component, it\'ll need to be client-side and use `useEffect` or Framer Motion for mouse tracking and the binary grid.\n\n\n**Generating Binary Grid**\n\nI am now generating the binary grid component. I will make a full-screen fixed grid of 0s and 1s. Then, I\'ll apply `mask-image: radial-gradient(400px circle at ${x}px ${y}px, black, transparent)` to it, and include it in `app/layout.tsx`. Finally, I will ensure that the user\'s edits to `projects.tsx` are preserved.\n\n\n**Finalizing Binary Grid**\n\nI\'ve finished the binary grid component! I\'ve incorporated Framer Motion for smooth mouse tracking and the flashlight effect. I\'ve optimized the binary text generation for screen filling. I\'m now fine-tuning the `mask-image` and color contrast. I\'ve also integrated this into the `app/layout.tsx`. Finally, I\'m ensuring all user modifications to the `projects.tsx` are still intact.\n\n\n**Refining Interactive Spotlight**\n\nOkay, I\'m integrating the updated binary spotlight. I need to ensure I\'m importing `useMotionTemplate` correctly to generate the flashlight effect. I\'m also planning to generate a massive binary string using a single `motion.div` to achieve the grid effect. I\'ll need to use `break-all text-justify` for it to render correctly. I\'m now updating `/app/layout.tsx` to include the `<BinarySpotlight />` and adjust the body classes for light and dark modes. I will make sure the `dark` class is removed from the `html` tag.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific UI element adjustments. I\'m adding a hydration check to `theme-toggle.tsx`. In the header, I\'m updating the \"Aly.\" logo dot color to neutral. For the hero section, I\'m swapping the amber background on buttons with neutral tones, updating hover states, and eliminating gradient backgrounds. I am also working on the about section.\n\n\n**Updating UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now going through the various components. For the experience section, I\'m updating `bg-amber-600`, hover states, and text colors. In the projects section, I\'m updating colors and preserving user edits. The blog section will also get its colors updated. Finally, I\'m updating the contact section\'s icons, buttons, and input styles. I\'ll need to remove `text-amber-600` and change `w-16 h-1 bg-amber-600 rounded` to `bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-neutral-100`. I\'m working on the binary spotlight component to optimize the mask, and use Spring to implement the flashlight effect!\n\n\n**Optimizing Binary Generation**\n\nI\'m now optimizing the binary grid generation and mouse tracking for the interactive spotlight. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and efficiency. I\'m using `useSpring` and `useMotionValue` for smooth cursor interaction and dynamic binary text generation using `Math.random()`. I\'m also addressing some performance considerations for the flashlight mask and adjusting the binary text to fill the screen correctly on different devices.\n\n\n**Refining Binary Spotlight**\n\nI\'m now refining the interactive binary spotlight\'s performance. The previous dynamic binary text generation using `Math.random()` might be slow. I\'m testing a static string repeated via CSS to see if it\'s more efficient, but will fallback to the array version if the former doesn\'t fill the space. I\'ll need to check the mask image for the flashlight effect, too.\n\n\n"
