  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Potential Causes**\n\nI\'m now digging deeper into potential causes, and have to see if anything else could be wrong. I\'ve ruled out the font size; `text-[11px] leading-[14px]` seems adequate. My next focus is on a `break-all` conflict when it encounters 50,000 characters.\n\n\n**Exploring Alternative Solutions**\n\nI\'m now investigating alternative solutions, and it looks like a repeating background or SVG might be the key. I am checking to see how to implement this, but the prompt\'s SVG requirement complicates things, even though it may resolve the lag issue. I\'ve ruled out the dark/light mode switch and the text color; the classes seem appropriate.\n\n\n**Analyzing Contrast Problems**\n\nI\'ve discovered the contrast is abysmal in light mode, as the text is nearly invisible. It\'s `neutral-400` at 20% opacity on `#fafafa`, which is a terrible combination. Dark mode is subtle, which I intended. I also checked for horizontal scrolling on the body, but it\'s not the container. I also removed colored backgrounds, which introduced transparency.\n\n\n**Examining Rendering Process**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering process. The `BinarySpotlight` component seems correct; it uses a standard pattern for SSR/client hydration. I\'m focusing on whether the 50,000-character text node, rendered in `useEffect` on the client, is the bottleneck. The array generation is quick, and text rendering is fast on modern browsers. However, `text-justify` and `break-all` might be an expensive combination on 50,000 chars. I will try pre-generating the text on the server or using just `break-all`.\n\n\n**Clarifying Event Handling**\n\nI\'m now clarifying event handling, as the `BinarySpotlight` might be interfering. I\'m focusing on its `pointer-events` settings within the `layout.tsx` file. The `pointer-events-none` class is on the outer div, but not explicitly on the inner `motion.div`. It looks like it doesn\'t inherit as expected. If so, then the `BinarySpotlight` would capture all mouse events, which is not what I intend.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 181587436
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
